@* Whether the stored snapshot has applied an event, as one mark on its row: a tick when it has, a
   clock when it has not yet — the same clock the version warning wears, because it says the same
   thing about one event that the warning says about the row: the history has moved past what was
   written. No word beside it, because the column has none above it either; the mark's title and
   label say it for a pointer and a screen reader.

   One component rather than a copy on each of the four detail pages: an event is applied or not
   the same way on a streamed model and a DCB one, and a reader should meet the same two marks on
   either. *@
<span class="@(Applied ? "applied" : "pending")"
      role="img"
      aria-label="@Label"
      title="@Label">
    @* Built to the box, stroke and linecap every other mark here is built to. *@
    <svg class="glyph" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"
         fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"
         stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        @if (Applied)
        {
            <path d="M4 10.5 8.2 14.5 16 6"/>
        }
        else
        {
            <circle cx="10" cy="10" r="7"/>
            <path d="M10 6.2V10l2.6 2"/>
        }
    </svg>
</span>

@code {

    /// <summary>Whether the stored snapshot has applied the row's event.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    [EditorRequired]
    public bool Applied { get; set; }

    private string Label => Applied
        ? "Applied to the stored snapshot"
        : "Not applied to the stored snapshot yet";

}
